00:22:25.053 --> 00:22:26.660
And like, we have to
get through this part.

00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:28.080
So you can get to this
part if you don't get

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:29.080
this part, you know?

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:31.810
So I think they're not too young

00:22:31.810 --> 00:22:34.010
to understand any of those things.

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:36.100
And we should never assume
that they're too young

00:22:36.100 --> 00:22:36.933
to understand those things.

00:22:36.933 --> 00:22:39.070
We should always at
least try to communicate

00:22:39.070 --> 00:22:41.270
to them, like the why
of what they're doing.

00:22:42.150 --> 00:22:43.400
- I agree, 100%.

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:45.050
I think it's so easy for us to assume

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:47.098
where five, six, seven, eight year olds,

00:22:47.098 --> 00:22:48.820
you know, that they don't think

00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:50.580
about how the world works, but they do.

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:52.557
And if you talk to them about jobs

00:22:52.557 --> 00:22:54.033
and the competitive workplace

00:22:54.033 --> 00:22:56.616
and how, and what skills you need

00:22:56.616 --> 00:22:58.570
to be able to participate, it's funny.

00:22:58.570 --> 00:23:00.240
I think there was this was many years ago.

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:01.830
It was like five or six years ago.

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:03.410
I got an email from a mother

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:04.750
and she had a picture of her child

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:06.310
