00:23:50.357 --> 00:23:52.559
"I don't get economically marginalized."

00:23:52.559 --> 00:23:54.172
(all laughing)

00:23:54.172 --> 00:23:57.070
I think he use words like almost
economically marginalized.

00:23:57.070 --> 00:23:58.890
So clearly a precocious kid

00:23:58.890 --> 00:24:00.490
using words like that at age seven.

00:24:00.490 --> 00:24:01.700
But he said something that felt like

00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:03.630
I wanna make sure that I don't get like,

00:24:03.630 --> 00:24:05.390
you know, automated out of the economy.

00:24:05.390 --> 00:24:07.720
So he definitely understood.

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:08.780
And that, that's kind of

00:24:08.780 --> 00:24:09.710
that I remember there's, you know,

00:24:09.710 --> 00:24:11.070
I'm dating myself, I'm, you know,

00:24:11.070 --> 00:24:12.520
there's a Karl Malone quote,

00:24:12.520 --> 00:24:14.745
famous basketball player
for the Utah Jazz.

00:24:14.745 --> 00:24:17.267
And he used to imagine, he used to say,

00:24:17.267 --> 00:24:19.887
"whenever I get tired,

00:24:19.887 --> 00:24:22.480
"I imagine that my
competitors are at the gym."

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:23.790
And I don't want that
to be like, you know,

00:24:23.790 --> 00:24:24.760
to stress people out,

00:24:24.760 --> 00:24:27.300
that you have to always
be like on top of it.

00:24:27.300 --> 00:24:29.300
But that can also be a
little bit of a motivator

00:24:29.300 --> 00:24:30.444
that like, you know look

00:24:30.444 --> 00:24:33.400
it's, you don't want your
kids to get stressed out,

00:24:33.400 --> 00:24:34.930
but you also don't want them to live

00:24:34.930 --> 00:24:36.370
in a reality where they think that,

00:24:36.370 --> 00:24:38.400
you know, actually I see this,

00:24:38.400 --> 00:24:40.750
the fire I grew up not so wealthy.

00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:42.400
So I had a little bit
of a fire in my belly.

00:24:42.400 --> 00:24:43.340
'Cause, you know, I could say, look,

00:24:43.340 --> 00:24:45.191
I wanna different standard of living.

00:24:45.191 --> 00:24:46.240
- I dint know that.

00:24:46.240 --> 00:24:48.240
- Oh yeah you know my mom,
- I didn't know that yeah

00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:49.410
- Oh no my mum you know,

00:24:49.410 --> 00:24:51.560
we were, you know she raised us by herself

00:24:51.560 --> 00:24:53.940
and she was a cashier at
some convenient stores.

00:24:53.940 --> 00:24:54.773
And you know,

00:24:54.773 --> 00:24:56.890
so she was the year I
went to apply to college.

00:24:56.890 --> 00:24:58.780
She was making 16,000 a year.

00:24:58.780 --> 00:25:01.130
But that, you know for me, that created

00:25:01.130 --> 00:25:02.720
