on my horrible parenting habits.

00:28:55.370 --> 00:28:56.670
So from Steven Cottrell,

00:28:56.670 --> 00:28:58.920
what are tips on developing
a sense of purpose

00:28:58.920 --> 00:29:00.140
among teenagers?

00:29:00.140 --> 00:29:01.288
Great question.

00:29:01.288 --> 00:29:04.390
- You know, one of the,
like, like less known,

00:29:04.390 --> 00:29:06.300
but I think really important facts

00:29:06.300 --> 00:29:08.520
about adolescents is that,

00:29:08.520 --> 00:29:12.920
you know, teenagers are
maybe more purpose driven

00:29:12.920 --> 00:29:16.500
during that period of
life than any other time.

00:29:16.500 --> 00:29:18.280
And so we have a stereotype

00:29:18.280 --> 00:29:21.874
of teenagers being selfish
and even narcissistic

00:29:21.874 --> 00:29:24.270
and really to the contrary,

00:29:24.270 --> 00:29:27.710
they're extremely motivated
by fairness by equity,

00:29:27.710 --> 00:29:29.313
by social change.

00:29:30.380 --> 00:29:33.710
I witnessed this myself with
my own 17 and 18 year old.

00:29:33.710 --> 00:29:36.600
I often get with mini lectures

00:29:36.600 --> 00:29:38.080
on how I have to, I think,

00:29:38.080 --> 00:29:39.360
like, I think of myself as someone

00:29:39.360 --> 00:29:41.120
