00:36:05.850 --> 00:36:07.500
they had to learn a lot of math

00:36:07.500 --> 00:36:08.580
and another condition,

00:36:08.580 --> 00:36:12.040
He, all he did was he
helped break down the math,

00:36:12.040 --> 00:36:15.980
the same math into sub
goals, into smaller parts.

00:36:15.980 --> 00:36:18.060
And there was a dramatic benefit

00:36:18.060 --> 00:36:19.900
and those kids did better.

00:36:19.900 --> 00:36:21.800
And I think the life
lesson, as you say Sal

00:36:21.800 --> 00:36:23.220
not only for kids, but for us

00:36:23.220 --> 00:36:24.440
is that when you have big things,

00:36:24.440 --> 00:36:25.720
you break them into small things.

00:36:25.720 --> 00:36:26.687
And when you take those small things

00:36:26.687 --> 00:36:28.350
and you break them even further,

00:36:28.350 --> 00:36:30.380
that's when I think you
really get momentum.

00:36:30.380 --> 00:36:32.240
And I'll just give one personal example.

00:36:32.240 --> 00:36:34.230
The hardest thing I
ever did professionally

00:36:34.230 --> 00:36:35.600
was to write my book.

00:36:35.600 --> 00:36:38.170
And when I thought about
like writing a book,

00:36:38.170 --> 00:36:39.470
it was like too big.

00:36:39.470 --> 00:36:41.620
Then I thought like, well,
I'll just work on chapter one

00:36:41.620 --> 00:36:42.660
still too big.

00:36:42.660 --> 00:36:43.493
Then I thought like, well,

00:36:43.493 --> 00:36:45.560
just work on like the
first half of chapter one

00:36:45.560 --> 00:36:46.393
still too big.

00:36:46.393 --> 00:36:48.130
And I found myself procrastinating

00:36:48.130 --> 00:36:51.184
and just never feeling like
I wanted to get started.

00:36:51.184 --> 00:36:53.130
Then finally I broke it
down to the smallest things

00:36:53.130 --> 00:36:58.045
like today, I'm gonna
write a sentence maybe.

00:36:58.045 --> 00:37:00.650
And what I meant by maybe is that like

00:37:00.650 --> 00:37:02.110
I might throw out that sentence

00:37:02.110 --> 00:37:03.902
and now I had broken
down the big thing a book

00:37:03.902 --> 00:37:05.680
into smaller things a chapter

00:37:05.680 --> 00:37:06.670
into smaller smarts.

00:37:06.670 --> 00:37:10.815
So that the thing that I
had to do that day was tiny.

00:37:10.815 --> 00:37:14.250
And actually, I think
that was a great strategy

00:37:14.250 --> 00:37:15.910
because once I wrote that sentence,

00:37:15.910 --> 00:37:18.280
I was like, well since I'm sitting here,

00:37:18.280 --> 00:37:20.450
I may as well write another one.

00:37:20.450 --> 00:37:23.120
And in general, I think
if we can help kids

00:37:23.120 --> 00:37:26.110
learn the skill of breaking down the big,

00:37:26.110 --> 00:37:28.670
into small and getting started,

00:37:28.670 --> 00:37:30.170
then we'll be actually a long way

00:37:30.170 --> 00:37:32.370
towards helping them
finish what they begin.

00:37:33.260 --> 00:37:34.530
- Yeah I couldn't agree more.

